  "sport": "bandy",
  "title": "Build-up from the throw-out with three players",
  "description": "Full rink with a goalkeeper in each goal. Three players start the build-up: A (forward or midfielder) by the left board in their own half, B (wide half) down by the end line on the right and C (forward or midfielder) on the right side up by the centre line.\n\nA skates down along the board, takes the goalkeeper's throw-out, carries the ball inside and hits a hard ball across to B, who has picked up speed from the end line. B carries the ball upfield and inside. C first skates towards their own goal to build up speed, turns and comes at full speed along the right board, where B plays the ball into their path. Then it is free play to goal with all three. The next trio starts from the other side.\n\nProgression: add one or two defenders in the opposition half. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Never stop after a pass – keep skating into the attack."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Watch the offside line: hold back by skating a wider curve instead of stopping."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "C only turns when the ball is on its way to B, so the speed is there when the pass arrives."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Play the pass in front of the receiver, into their skating line."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
